                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really wanted to like this game and even had it on my wishlist.\nWith some minor tweaks it's (my) worst point could be improved.\n\nPositive:\nThe basic concept is quite cool, depending on your choices new dialogs are unlocked and the endings are choosen.\n\nNeutral / semi negative:\nIn the first few moments you're intotruced to a lot of characters and their storys (more text).\nPartially these good-okay, some are not that interesting and the humor to try hard at some points.\n\nNegative:\nI tried to start a guide for this game and probably the reason why none exists:\nIt's very hard to track your decisions that affect the ending.\n\nWhile during the talking phase you get to know the topic.\nFor example talk with [i]Dustin about All-Star[/i] but in the end you only get [i]Dustin 1, 2, 5, ...[/i] for every piece of unlocked\ndialog.\nSome dialogs have to be avoided for certain endings but this system gives you no obvious clues, like 1 or 2 additional UI elements if it could have certain effects.\nIf you don't want to choose them all or randomly your options only are to re-read and think for yourself if you want to choose them or not, which becomes just annoying if you do multiple playtrhoughs and try to unlock certain endings (end then still fail).\n\nAlso in one playthrough you can only cover a small portion of dialogs, some of they are just wasted time/traps where others would have been a better choice.",
